  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nA prolonged period of dry weather is expected through the workweek \nand even through the weekend as high pressure anchors over the \neastern CONUS. Highs will be in the 60s each day with lows in the \n30s and lower 40s each night. Efficient radiational cooling and \nlight winds will result in patchy to areas of frost in the eastern \nhalf of the area tonight and possibly each night through the \nremainder of the week, but most of the frost will occur in locations \nwhere the growing season has ended. Will need to keep an eye on the \nfrost coverage typical cold spots of Ashland/Holmes/Wayne counties \ntonight into early Tuesday morning, where the growing season has not \nyet ended. A localized Frost Advisory may be needed. Temperatures \nmay begin to warm into the 70s as the high shifts east towa rds the \nend of the weekend.",
